      "title": "SCC Factbook Report",
      "url": "https://scc.losrios.edu/scc/main/doc/1-Why-SCC/4-Facts-and-Statistics/Factbook-Report.pdf",
      "summary": "The SCC Factbook Report for the academic year 2018-19 provides a comprehensive snapshot of the student population at Sacramento City College. It covers several key metrics such as total enrollment which was 21,881 in Fall 2018, student demographics including age, gender, and ethnicity distributions, and educational goals. More than 45% of students are continuing students and primarily attend part-time, with 34% taking 12 or more units. The report highlights that the student body is ethnically diverse, with Hispanic/Latinos comprising about 33%. Over 57% of students attend day classes, and 20% are seeking work. The most popular majors among new students include general education transfer, pre-allied health & nursing, and biology. It also examines geographic distribution of students, noting several common feeder high schools and prominent zip codes. The report utilizes data including contributions from UC Davis students.",
      "stored": false,
      "fetched_at": "2026-05-25T19:18:10.904215+05:30"
    },
    {
      "doc_type": "strategic_plan",
      "year": 2023,
      "title": "Sacramento City College Strategic Plan 2023-2027",
      "url": "https://inside.scc.losrios.edu/scc/inside/doc/e4-planning-and-research/planning/scc-strategic-master-plan.pdf",
      "summary": "The Sacramento City College Strategic Plan 2023-2027 outlines a comprehensive roadmap to enhance access, success, and equity within the institution. It aims to improve enrollment processes, increase course offerings, and develop student-focused research strategies. The plan sets clear targets to reduce energy and water usage and promote sustainability through academic programs and infrastructure improvements.",
      "stored": false,
